      "title": "Bridging the \"New World Disorder\"",
      "description": "A collaborative international initiative designed to counter rising geopolitical fragmentation and armed conflict by mobilizing independent experts, civil society leaders, and community peacebuilders. The program utilizes informal diplomacy to keep communication channels open between regions experiencing severe political breakdown. Through structured dialogue and regional workshops, participants develop practical, citizen-driven peace blueprints that can be presented to formal governing bodies. By shifting focus from hostile rhetoric to shared human security, the initiative empowers local actors to build sustainable foundations for long-term conflict resolution.",
      "status": "proposal",
      "lifecyclePhase": "projected",
      "visibility": {
        "policy": "public"
      },
